<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Samo</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. c. 658</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Samo was a Frankish merchant who, according to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chronicle-of-fredegar">Chronicle of Fredegar</a>, led the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slavs">Slavs</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-europe">Central Europe</a> in a revolt against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/avars">Avars</a> around 623 and was then chosen as their king, ruling for some thirty-five years. In about 631 he defeated the Frankish king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dagobert-i">Dagobert I</a> at Wogastisburg. His realm, probably centred in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moravia">Moravia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bohemia">Bohemia</a> or <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lower-austria">Lower Austria</a>, is the first known Slavic polity.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/samo.jpg" alt="Samo" width="320" height="237" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Palickap · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:N%C3%A1klo_(vrch),_S%C3%A1mo_(2).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
